FINDINGS:
1. [BLOCKER] SPEC.md:1016 — claims `ask` is an ordinary identifier and nothing reads input, but src/runtime.rs:787 implements `"input" | "ask" => read_line(args, span)` reading stdin — spec is false and the new test pins the refusal instead of fixing the registration — register `ask`/`input` in `stdlib::BUILTIN_NAMES`/`builtins()` or remove the runtime arm and its `read_line` helper.
2. [MAJOR] src/runtime.rs:731 — `input.pop()` unconditionally drops the last character, so EOF without a trailing newline truncates data (`"abc"` becomes `"ab"`) — only strip a trailing `\n`/`\r\n` instead of popping blindly.
3. [MAJOR] src/runtime.rs:779 — `length` on text uses `s.len()` (bytes) while src/stdlib.rs:454 uses `s.chars().count()` (characters), so `length("é")` is 2 via `runtime::builtin` and 1 via `builtin_function` — make both agree on characters and pin `length("é")` to `1`.
4. [MAJOR] tests/stdlib_module_docs_test.rs:310 — `let _ = ok;` discards exit status and only checks `!stderr.contains("Unknown function")`, so a builtin that always errors still passes — assert the refused-by-name error or drop the surface walk.
5. [MAJOR] src/stdlib.rs:50 — `modules_without_functions()` uses `.any()` for a `<module>_` prefix, so one stub (e.g. `list_map` for `list`) hides missing members like `list.filter`/`list.reduce` — require each documented member or fail on alias-resolved-only modules.
6. [MAJOR] tests/stdlib_module_names_test.rs:392 — loopback server assumes direct `127.0.0.1` access while src/runtime.rs:1367 builds the client with proxy env enabled, so `HTTP_PROXY` routes the test request away and fails green CI — clear proxy env in the test or set `.no_proxy()` on the client.
